Some months ago, a discussion took place about what (if any) items
were essential to winning the game.  Your's truly argued at that
time that while speed boots were the author's personal favorite as
the most powerful items in the games, the only truly essential
item was either a cloak of magic resistance or gray dragon scale mail
in order to ward of Finger of Death from the Wizard of Yendor.

Old and Brand New Spoiler Follows-

During a posting about named weapons, I mentioned that it was a good
idea to polymorph into a Vampire Lord before attacking the Wizard.
That will make you immune to Finger of Death, since you're already (un)dead.


Curiously enough, there is another way to defend against F.O.D.
The BRAND NEW SPOILER is: If you are fighting the Wizard, and cannot
polymorph into an undead creature, and don't have magic resistant armor,
you can quaff a potion of hallucination (!) to protect yourself!
If the Wiz tries F.O.D. you get an "out of body experience", but are
otherwise unharmed.  Who'd a thunk it?

Conclusion: There are enough methods in this game to allow for winning
with whatever objects come to hand.

P.S. Speed boots are still #1 in my book :-)


